summary:
- topic: Meeting Opening and Budget Referendum
  text: The special meeting commenced with a call to order, roll call, and the Pledge
    of Allegiance. Board Chair Rosemarie DeAngelis and Superintendent Angela Atkinson
    Duina expressed gratitude to South Portland voters for their overwhelming support
    of the recent budget referendum.
- topic: Personnel Recognition and Appointment
  text: Superintendent Angela Atkinson Duina recognized Kelly Perkins, a long-serving
    clerk at Brown Elementary, for her retirement and significant contributions to
    the district. The board also unanimously approved the appointment of Ashley Peterson
    as a 3rd-grade teacher at Kaler Elementary.
- topic: Executive Sessions
  text: 'The board entered two executive sessions: one to discuss a labor relations
    matter involving the South Portland Educational Support Professionals Association
    (SPESPA) and another for a confidential personnel matter.'
- topic: SPESPA Tentative Agreement
  text: Following the first executive session, the board unanimously approved a tentative
    agreement reached with the South Portland Educational Support Professionals Association
    concerning an apprentice dispute, authorizing the chair to execute the memorandum
    of agreement.
- topic: Interim Superintendent Search Initiation
  text: The agenda was amended to include action on the search for an interim superintendent.
    The board discussed the importance of ensuring leadership consistency and minimizing
    transitions for the district.
- topic: Authorization for Interim Superintendent Search
  text: The board unanimously authorized the Maine School Management Association to
    assist with the search for an interim superintendent. This step aims to facilitate
    a thorough and timely process for securing temporary leadership.
- topic: Superintendent Matheney Separation Agreement
  text: The board unanimously authorized the board chair and legal counsel to negotiate
    a separation agreement with Superintendent Matheney. This action is contingent
    upon the successful completion of the interim superintendent search.
